# Bark-Knuckle Boxer: mana paid for an additional cost counts toward expend (CR 700.14, 601.2f-h; the expend ruling on
# changed costs). The Boxer is mana 1-2; Bloodchief's Thirst kicked is mana 3-6, so casting it expends 4 and the trigger
# resolves first: the Boxer gains indestructible and the Thirst aimed at it destroys nothing (CR 702.12b). Unkicked it would
# be only the third mana (the other scenario).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Bark-Knuckle Boxer
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Bloodchief's Thirst
Forest
Forest x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bark-Knuckle Boxer.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bloodchief's Thirst.Cast(Kicked: 1)
Bot1.Target(Bark-Knuckle Boxer)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Bark-Knuckle Boxer.Keywords = Indestructible
[T2 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Bark-Knuckle Boxer.Keywords = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Bloodchief's Thirst; Black Lotus
